From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:17:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 58/59] drama: a voice file can hold several references, spoken
 in order

drama3-voice/2 carries one source and an ordered references list, each entry a passage's text, codes, codes digest and clip audio_sha256, checked as a single-reference file is. A voice's references go through the same lowering and build_prompt_rows as a request's, so a /2 voice [A, B, C] builds the rows of a request sending A and B for a voice holding C; a /1 file builds the prompt it did. /2 is a new format so a loader that reads only /1 refuses the file instead of speaking from one passage. A voice whose references leave no prompt row for an input stops the server at startup, by name. drama_voice.py combine joins voice files of one source kind, copying their codes unchanged. GET /v1/voices reports each voice's reference count.
